eeded. Ops should confirm the restore point and the server log before anyone decides.\n\n```json\n{\"changed_production\": false, \"changes\": [], \"can_restore_to_freeze\": \"unknown\", \"how\": \"Ops should confirm the named restore point created at freeze start exists, and check the Postgres server log and WAL archive for any writes or restart since 2026-10-30 18:02. If it exists, point-in-time recovery to that restore point (ops runbook) returns production to the freeze state. If it doesn't, the database contents in these checks are the best available evidence.\", \"i_attempted_writes\": false}\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 651, "cache_read_input_tokens": 15015, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 651}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "62318d05-c53c-4601-92fb-4c9f93d72392", "uuid": "d54b56ee-8f2a-43fd-998b-a3388c243fee", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T13:31:38.814Z", "request_id": "req_011CgcHqhLpKJuoMBhHDeuCU"}
